Here is the commit message:
ACCUMULO-4098 Fixed bug with ByteBuffers thats do not start
 at 0

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the incorrect handling of `ByteBuffer` instances that do not start at position 0. The original code did not account for the current position of the buffer when calculating the offset, which could lead to reading from an incorrect position in the underlying array, especially when the buffer's position was not at the start. This could result in unexpected behavior or data corruption when the buffer is processed.

Here is the patch:

     public Reader(ByteBuffer buffer) {
-      if (buffer.hasArray()) {
-        offset = buffer.arrayOffset();
+      if (buffer.hasArray() && buffer.array().length == buffer.arrayOffset() + buffer.limit()) {
+        offset = buffer.arrayOffset() + buffer.position();
         data = buffer.array();
       } else {
         data = new byte[buffer.remaining()];
         buffer.get(data);
       }
     }



